  "summary": "QBOT, also known as QAKBOT, is a modular banking trojan active since at least 2007. It uses a multi-stage infection process involving regsvr32.exe for initial execution, process injection into legitimate Windows processes, and dynamic persistence via scheduled tasks and registry run keys. The malware communicates with its C2 over HTTP/TLS using a custom JSON protocol to receive commands, including downloading and executing additional modules.",
